cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenRelTime, please cite this software and the RelTime
  methodology papers it implements.
title: OpenRelTime
authors:
  - name: "曾子超"
    email: "zengzichao@sjtu.edu.cn"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6553-970X"
  - name: "王寅炤"
    email: "wyz@sjtu.edu.cn"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8715-1386"
version: 0.1.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23053146"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZengZichao/OpenRelTime"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
funding: >-
  This work was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China
  [grant numbers 42422209, 42272354] and the National Key Research and
  Development Program of China [grant number 2023YFC3108600].
abstract: >-
  OpenRelTime is an open-source Python implementation of the relative rate
  framework (RRF) for non-Bayesian molecular dating, including calibration
  conversion, analytical confidence intervals, CorrTest rate-autocorrelation
  testing, birth-death prior (ddBD) estimation and a bag-of-little-bootstraps
  pipeline.
keywords:
  - molecular dating
  - relative rate framework
  - phylogenetics
  - timetree
  - CorrTest
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Theoretical foundation of the RelTime method for estimating divergence times
      from variable evolutionary rates
    authors:
      - name: Koichiro Tamura
      - name: Qiqing Tao
      - name: Sudhir Kumar
    journal: Molecular Biology and Evolution
    volume: 35
    pages: "1770-1782"
    year: 2018
    doi: 10.1093/molbev/msy044
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Reliable confidence intervals for RelTime estimates of evolutionary
      divergence times
    authors:
      - name: Qiqing Tao
      - name: Koichiro Tamura
      - name: Beatriz Mello
      - name: Sudhir Kumar
    journal: Molecular Biology and Evolution
